                            <comment id="15725286" author="iveselovskiy" created="Tue, 6 Dec 2016 12:02:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;pull request&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1320&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1320&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15735617" author="vozerov" created="Fri, 9 Dec 2016 15:37:56 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ivan,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Patch looks good to me, but we need to ensure that it works on the following environments:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Apache Hadoop&lt;br/&gt;
2) HDP&lt;br/&gt;
3) CDH&lt;br/&gt;
4) MapR&lt;br/&gt;
5) In addition let&apos;s check that it works in Windows env w/ Apache Hadoop.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15745832" author="iveselovskiy" created="Tue, 13 Dec 2016 18:20:56 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Tested on Apache 2.7.0,  HDP 2.4, Cloudera  5.3.0, MapR 5.2.0.&lt;br/&gt;
Windows case not applicable there since Hadoop does not contein .dll libraries  for Windows , and thus &quot;ignite.bat&quot; script not affected by the change at all. Even if somebody runs &quot;ignite.sh&quot; on Windows, no harm is there , since lib/native/  contains only Unix libraries that will not be loaded on Windows. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
